From: RCTools GPU audit
Subject: [PATCH] faker: add surfaceless EGL backend for Qualcomm KGSL

Base: VirtualGL/virtualgl
Commit: 2473cf39bdbe88ca41ecd58ac4007385c9682a9f

VirtualGL's EGL back end normally enumerates EGLDevice objects and therefore
expects a DRM device/render node.  Mesa's Freedreno KGSL path on Android-style
kernels instead uses /dev/kgsl-3d0 and EGL_PLATFORM_SURFACELESS_MESA, so the
Adreno 506 in DroidSpaces is not discoverable as an EGLDevice.

Treat VGL_DISPLAY=eglkgsl as an explicit project-specific request for a
surfaceless EGL display.  Keep all existing EGLDevice behavior unchanged for
"egl", "eglN", and DRI device paths.

The resulting display is still required to expose
EGL_KHR_no_config_context and EGL_KHR_surfaceless_context, matching the
requirements of VirtualGL's existing EGL back end.

diff --git a/server/faker.cpp b/server/faker.cpp
--- a/server/faker.cpp
+++ b/server/faker.cpp
@@
